  "title": "Cyprus (island)",
  "provenance": "Barrington Atlas: BAtlas 72 C2 Cyprus Ins.",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/island"
  ],
  "details": "<p>Two mountain ranges, the Trogodos and Kyrenia Mountains, and a central plain are the major physical features of Cyprus. Human settlement is dated to 10,000 BC. Mycenaean Greeks, Syrians, and Phoenicians all established settlements prior to the Classical period.</p>\r\n<p>The later <a href=\"../981516\">Roman province of Cyprus</a> is a separate place.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Cyprus is the third largest island in the Mediterranean Sea.",
